@page
@model Typebeat.Web.Pages.Legal.PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy policy";
}

<div class="stack prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>

    <p class="muted">Last updated 26 September 2026.</p>

    <p>
        type!beat is a free lyric-typing rhythm game and this website (typebeat.mingda.sh) is its
        online service: accounts, leaderboards, replays and beatmap sharing. This page explains what
        we store about you, why, and how to get rid of it. Questions go to
        <a href="mailto:contact@mingda.sh">contact@mingda.sh</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="card">
        <h3 class="card-title">What we store</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Your account:</strong> username, email address, and a salted hash of your password (never the password itself). Optionally a profile picture, cover image, "about me" text and country, if you add them.</li>
            <li><strong>Google sign-in:</strong> if you use "Continue with Google", we receive your Google account ID, email address and whether Google has verified it, and your display name (used only to suggest a username). We do not receive your Google password, contacts, files or anything else, and we never post to or act on your Google account.</li>
            <li><strong>Gameplay:</strong> the scores and replays you submit, with their mods, statistics and timestamps; which beatmaps you download, favourite or pin; which replays you watch.</li>
            <li><strong>Things you upload:</strong> beatmaps (lyrics, timing, audio and artwork) and any reports you file.</li>
            <li><strong>Sign-in state:</strong> short-lived codes we email you, and session tokens for the website and the game.</li>
            <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> the web server records requests (including IP address and browser) for security and debugging. These logs are rotated and not kept long-term, and are not used to build profiles of anyone.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3 class="card-title">What is public</h3>
        <p>
            Your username, profile picture, cover, "about me", country, scores, replays, rankings and
            uploaded beatmaps are shown publicly on the site, in the game and in the type!beat
            Discord. Your email address and anything tied to Google sign-in are never shown to other
            players.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3 class="card-title">Cookies</h3>
        <p>
            We only use cookies needed to sign you in and keep you signed in (a session cookie, plus
            short-lived encrypted cookies during an email-code or Google sign-in). There are no
            advertising cookies, no analytics or tracking scripts, and nothing is shared with ad
            networks.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3 class="card-title">Who else handles your data</h3>
        <p>We do not sell your data. A few services process it on our behalf, only to run the site:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Hetzner</strong> hosts the servers and database.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> sits in front of the site for security and caching.</li>
            <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers our emails (sign-in codes, password resets).</li>
            <li><strong>Sentry</strong> receives crash reports when something breaks, configured not to include personal data.</li>
            <li><strong>Google</strong> handles sign-in when you choose "Continue with Google".</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3 class="card-title">Google user data</h3>
        <p>
            Data received from Google is used only to sign you in and to link your Google account to
            your type!beat account. It is not used for advertising, not sold, and not shared with
            anyone except as needed to run the service. You can unlink Google in
            <a href="/settings">Settings</a> (once your account has a password), or revoke type!beat's
            access from your Google account's security settings at any time.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3 class="card-title">Deleting your account</h3>
        <p>
            You can delete your account yourself in <a href="/settings">Settings</a>. This removes
            your email, password, Google link, profile details, favourites, pins, download and
            watch history, and sign-in tokens. Your scores and uploaded beatmaps stay on the
            leaderboards so other players' rankings are not disturbed, but they are anonymised and
            no longer connected to you. If you can't sign in, email
            <a href="mailto:contact@mingda.sh">contact@mingda.sh</a> from your account's address
            and we'll do it for you. You can also ask us for a copy of the data we hold about you.
        </p>
    </div>

    <p class="muted">
        type!beat is not directed at children under 13. If this policy changes in a meaningful way,
        the date at the top will change and we'll say so on the site or in the Discord.
    </p>
</div>
